Evaluate $\int_{1}^{3}(x+2)\,dx$ using the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=0.65cm]
\definecolor{regionblue}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[regionblue] (1,0) -- (1,3) -- (3,5) -- (3,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->,black] (-0.3,0) -- (3.8,0);
\draw[->,black] (0,-0.3) -- (0,6);
\draw[black,thick] (0,2) -- (3.5,5.5);
\draw[black] (1,0) -- (1,3);
\draw[black] (3,0) -- (3,5);
\path (3.8,0) node[right,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$x$};
\path (0,6) node[above,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$y$};
\path (1,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$1$};
\path (3,0) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$3$};
\path (0,2) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$2$};
\path (1.8,5.4) node[font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {$y=x+2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
